<!--Post: 3112--><!--Time: 1104464188-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3112"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 7:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting.  My top candidate for BTK lives quite close to there &#40;exact distance withheld from BTK&#39;s prying eyes&#41;.  If you have a cell phone, you might consider upgrading to a cam-phone for your next outing to BK.  Nothing wrong with taking a few pictures of your kid having a good time at BK. <BR> <BR>Poor BTK.  He&#39;ll see this post.  If it is him, and he&#39;s a regular as skov suggests &#40;I agree 100%&#41;, and he stops going there now, they&#39;ll notice.  If he keeps going there, he&#39;s gonna risk being spotted again. <BR> <BR>Justice.  It&#39;s time for BTK to start feeling the heat.  And living in fear. <BR> <BR>Something else is apparent - the golf course next to the BK.  Several of BTK&#39;s victims lived almost adjacent to what appear to be open &#40;non-residence&#41; tracts in the middle of residential areas.  I can&#39;t tell what they are from the maps.  Like Skov, I&#39;m not in the immediate neighborhood.  Possibly no connection, but it&#39;s interesting, this proximity to open areas.  There&#39;s something he likes about that. <BR> <BR>And the golf-ball cap.  I find that very interesting, too.  I think that&#39;s why he was at that BK.  Golf is the perfect late-life/retirement sport for an active type like BTK.  BTK can flee BK - but would he give up his favorite hobby if you did spot him?  Join a new club?  Or will he brazen it out?  I didn&#39;t buy the hunting/fishing/camping thing in his recent bogus confessions for a second.  I&#39;d be looking at golf/skiing/sailing/hiking.  Bingo. <BR> <BR>Time will tell.... <BR> <BR>Could be a good lead!  pax56<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3112-->
<!--Post: 3119--><!--Time: 1104469113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3119"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 8:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cougar, Your not saying Smokey Robinson is BTK are you? jk <BR> <BR>B2K<!--/Text--></td></tr>
