<!--Post: 3129--><!--Time: 1104473868-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3129"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->COUGAR: Sorry to disagree, but it just sounds like an old man killing time at a fast-food restaurant. I&#39;ve seen HUNDREDS of them in fast-food joints all my life. It&#39;s a cheap &amp; easy way for an elderly guy to hang out in public, get some walking excercise, catch up on the latest newspaper articles, etc. <BR> <BR>I know we all want to catch the culprit A.S.A.P. but just looking like an old white guy that some psychic THINKS might look like BLT is not really very solid evidence to go on. <BR> <BR>Now, if he ordered a BLT with chesse, well then, NOW you&#39;re cooking with gas!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3129-->
<!--Post: 3134--><!--Time: 1104479101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3134"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 11:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Did you say the _psychic&#39;s_ sketch, V? Ooooooooo....... sorry, I&#39;ll take that back.  That would be a bit of a stretch, even for me &#40;although I have to tell you, Cougar - the psychic&#39;s sketch actually does look a lot like my guy.....I&#39;m _not_ kidding!&#41;.  Truthfully, I assumed you were talking about an age progression on a witness sketch.  My bad.  If looking like a badly dressed old white guy in BK were a crime, I&#39;d be busted.  I&#39;ll see if I can get the egg back on my Croissandwich.... &#40;&#40;pax&#41;&#41; &#40;forbidden blushing emoticon deleted&#41; <BR> <BR>PS - Is there a legitimate age-progression sketch out there?  I know the earlier descriptions and the one Otero sketch I saw were terrible, so don&#39;t know if it would be helpful....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3134-->
<!--Post: 3145--><!--Time: 1104510837-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3145"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 8:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As far as I know, a &#34;legitimate sketch&#34; does not exist.  <BR> <BR>I think my two year old needs another SpongeBob trinket. We&#39;ll go back to the BK today and see if he&#39;s there - might ask an employee if they remember him if he&#39;s not. Nothing ventured, nothing gained, right? Besides, I hate housework, lol. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3145-->
<!--Post: 3193--><!--Time: 1104602924-->
